## Part 1 — Data Pipeline — DONE

### 1.1 Raw data structure — DONE

Each yearly CSV (`data/raw/2010.csv` … `data/raw/2025.csv`) has these columns:

| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|------|-------|
| TEHNOYLEVAATUSPUNKT | str | Inspection station full name |
| PUNKTI_KOOD | str | Station code (2 letters, e.g. "HA", "MM") |
| TOOTAJA | str | Inspector employee ID |
| YV_KUUPAEV | str | Inspection year-month (YYYY-MM) |
| YLEVAATUSLIIK | str | KORRALINE / KORDUV / EURO6 / RAHVUSVAHELINE |
| YLEVAATUSOTSUS | str | KORRAS (pass) / KORDUVALE (fail) / VASTAB_NOUETELE |
| RIKKED | str | Defects: "SEVERITY:ID,SEVERITY:ID" — VO=minor, OV=significant, EOV=dangerous |
| SOIDUK_ID | int | Anonymised vehicle ID |
| ESMANE_REG_AASTA | int | First registration year |
| MARK | str | Vehicle make (e.g. VOLKSWAGEN) |
| MUDEL | str | Vehicle model |
| KATEGOORIA | str | Vehicle category (M1, N1, O1, L3e, …) |
| KERETYYP | str | Body type (SEDAAN, UNIVERSAAL, KAUBIK, …) |

The defect lookup table (`data/raw/rike.csv`) maps defect IDs to descriptions.
Key columns: ID (int), NIMETUS (str, defect name in Estonian), TYYP (GRUPP/ALAMGRUPP/NIMETUS), VO/OV/EOV (Jah/Ei).

> **Implementation note:** Data is NOT downloaded to disk. `src/data_loader.py` reads all 16 years (2010–2025) directly from remote URLs via DuckDB. `rike.csv` is the only file tracked in `data/raw/` (git exception in `.gitignore`).

### 1.2 Encoding issue — DONE

Many strings are mojibake (UTF-8 read as Latin-1). Fix by encoding to latin-1 then decoding as utf-8:

```python
text.encode("latin-1").decode("utf-8")
```

Applied in `src/data_loader.py` via `_fix_encoding()` at module load time. Also applied to `rike.csv` defect names when building `_RIKE_LOOKUP`.

### 1.3 Derived columns — DONE

All derived columns are computed at query time inside DuckDB SQL in `src/data_loader.py`. `src/data_cleaner.py` also implements them for local batch use (requires downloading CSVs first).

- `YV_AASTA` / `YV_KUU` — parsed from YV_KUUPAEV in each query
- `VANUS` — computed inline: `CAST(SUBSTR(YV_KUUPAEV,1,4) AS INT) - CAST(ESMANE_REG_AASTA AS INT)`
- `RIKETE_ARV`, `VO_ARV`, `OV_ARV`, `EOV_ARV` — via `STRING_SPLIT` + `UNNEST` in DuckDB
- `RIKE_IDS` — extracted per-query where needed
- `LABIS_ESIMESEL` — `CASE WHEN YLEVAATUSOTSUS='KORRAS' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END` (KORRALINE only)
- `PUNKTI_RANGUS` — computed as station fail rate in `q_station_strictness()`
- `ANDMED_PUUDULIKUD` — implemented in `data_cleaner.py` for local pipeline

